# Get started

This repository is a Dart pub workspace named **zonai**. Use the pinned Flutter/Dart SDK via **FVM** so versions match the team and `pubspec.yaml` constraints.

## Prerequisites

- [Git](https://git-scm.com/)
- [FVM](https://fvm.app/) (Flutter Version Management)

## 1. Clone and submodules

```bash
git clone <repository-url> zonai
cd zonai
git submodule update --init --recursive
```

The **raindrop** ORM lives under `libs/raindrop` as a submodule, pinned to the **`zonai`** branch on the fork [mrgnhnt96/raindrop](https://github.com/mrgnhnt96/raindrop). The original project is [wolfenrain/raindrop](https://github.com/wolfenrain/raindrop); inside the submodule, `origin` is the fork and `upstream` is wolfenrain. The fork’s repo root is a separate Dart workspace; checking out only `packages/` avoids a conflict with this monorepo’s workspace resolution (“stray pubspec”). Run:

```bash
./tool/setup_raindrop_submodule.sh
```

Run this after clone, or whenever `libs/raindrop` looks like a full upstream checkout again (for example after `git submodule update` without sparse checkout). The script initializes the submodule if needed and applies the sparse-checkout rules.

## 2. Flutter / Dart SDK (FVM)

This project pins a Flutter version under `.fvm/` (see `.fvm/fvm_config.json`). Install and use it from the repo root:

```bash
fvm install
fvm use
```

If `fvm use` reports the version is already installed, you can skip `fvm install`.

## 3. Dependencies

Resolve the whole workspace from the repository root:

```bash
fvm dart pub get
```

## 4. App configs and env flavors

When you work on a Zonai app (e.g. `apps/playground`), you can maintain multiple **app config** Dart files and **`.env`** files for different targets (dev, staging, prod). Pass `--flavor <name>` to select which config file and which `.env.<flavor>` file to use.

See **[config-and-env-flavors.md](config-and-env-flavors.md)** for naming rules, precedence, and examples.

## 5. Optional checks

- Run CLI package tests:

  ```bash
  fvm dart test apps/cli
  ```

- **Infra / env tooling** (`pnv`) is declared in `support/infra`; use that package’s workflows when you work on infrastructure.

## Troubleshooting

- **`Found a pubspec.yaml ... stray`** near `libs/raindrop`: run `./tool/setup_raindrop_submodule.sh` so the raindrop root `pubspec.yaml` is not present beside `packages/`.
- **SDK version errors**: ensure you are using `fvm dart` / `fvm flutter`, not a mismatched global SDK.
